@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-5" dir="ltr">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
        Last updated: October 2, 2026
    </p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>

    <p>
        LogiCore ("we", "our", or "the application") respects your privacy.
        This Privacy Policy explains how LogiCore accesses, uses, stores,
        and protects information when you use our application.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>
        Depending on the features you use, LogiCore may process information
        provided by you, such as your name, email address, and account
        information required to authenticate you.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Google Account Information</h2>

    <p>
        LogiCore uses Google OAuth to allow users to sign in with their
        Google Account.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you authorize Google access, the application may receive basic
        account information such as your name, email address, and profile
        information that Google makes available through the requested
        permissions.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Google Drive Data</h2>

    <p>
        LogiCore may use the Google Drive API to provide features that require
        access to files created or used by the application.
    </p>

    <p>
        The application requests only the Google Drive permissions necessary
        for its functionality. Google Drive data accessed by LogiCore is used
        only to provide the features requested by the user.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How We Use Information</h2>

    <p>
        We use the information we access to:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Authenticate users.</li>
        <li>Provide application functionality.</li>
        <li>Provide Google Drive related features requested by the user.</li>
        <li>Maintain and improve the application.</li>
        <li>Protect the security and integrity of the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>

    <p>
        We do not sell users' personal information or Google user data.
        We do not share Google user data with third parties except where
        necessary to provide the requested functionality, comply with legal
        obligations, or protect the security of the service.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Storage and Security</h2>

    <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect
        information processed by the application against unauthorized access,
        alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        We retain information only for as long as necessary to provide the
        application's services or as required by applicable obligations.
        Users may request deletion of their applicable personal information
        by contacting us.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>

    <p>
        LogiCore's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs
        will comply with the Google API Services User Data Policy, including
        the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will
        be published on this page with an updated revision date.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>

    <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Email:</strong>
        elmansoryassel@gmail.com
    </p>
</div>
